All fixed and verified. Summary of what was wrong and what I changed:

Root cause of the failure (test_streaming_mid_line_always_immediate): in the new unmatched_marker_start helper, each backtick toggled the open-code-span state. Mid-line "" toggled open→close→open, leaving a phantom unmatched    in the carry buffer. The next token ("#") was then combined into the carry as "inside an open code span" and returned empty output — violating the pre-existing mid-line immediacy guarantee.

Fixes:
1. src/format/markdown.rs — unmatched_marker_start now treats a run of ≥3 backticks as fence-like literal text and skips it without toggling the open-tick state (runs of 1–2 behave exactly as before). ""` mid-line renders immediately with no carry.
2. Added `test_md_triple_backtick_mid_line_does_not_carry pinning the regression (both the helper returning None for "" and the token-after-` immediacy).
3. tests/module_size.rs — the ceiling bump required by step 3 of the task had never been done (entry was still 2932; file is now 3160), so the integration test would have failed next once the unit failure was cleared. Raised to 3160 with the dated // Day 162 (#661) comment per the #692 precedent.

Verification: cargo fmt ✓, cargo build ✓, cargo test ✓ (4666 passed unit + all integration suites including module_size), `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` ✓, `cargo fmt -- --check` ✓. All #661 carry tests, the latency-budget test, and the fence tests are green, unmodified.
